Inspect how proposals, votes, identifiers and certificates are created and verified.

A resulting state root alone does not identify the complete proposal that validators approved.

Two different operations must not be treated as the same proposal merely because they happen to result in the same state root.

Introduce a canonical complete proposal digest

Create a versioned, domain-separated canonical proposal serialization.

Its digest must commit to all execution-relevant content, including:

* Network ID.
* Genesis hash.
* Protocol version.
* Proposal version.
